Upstream projects (attribution)

This distribution is an integration of the following Apache-2.0 projects.
Their original copyright notices are preserved here.

1) NFrp / Rust-Frp -- https://github.com/Nu0vo1212/Rust-Frp
   Copyright 2026 nfrp contributors
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Used as the Rust protocol base: the `common`, `server` and `client` crates
   (frp v1/v2 wire protocol, TOML / legacy INI config compatibility, TLS,
   WebSocket, KCP, QUIC, yamux, dashboard, ACL, etc.). Files in those crates
   retain their original Apache-2.0 headers.

2) frp-wss-ipgeo -- https://github.com/wengjing086/frp-wss-ipgeo
   Copyright 2026 wengjing086
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   The WSS design (sniff `GET /~!frp` AFTER TLS decryption, replay the peeked
   bytes on mismatch) has been re-implemented in Rust in `server/src/serve.rs`.
   No Go source code is included.

3) frp-ip4p -- https://github.com/wengjing086/frp-ip4p
   Copyright 2026 wengjing086
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   The IP4P resolution rules (DNS TXT base64/plaintext "IP:port" -> IP4P AAAA
   2001:0000::/16 -> fallback, override serverPort) have been re-implemented in
   Rust in `common/src/ip4p.rs`. No Go source code is included.
   The IP4P concept originates from hevz/frp (ip4p branch, Apache-2.0) and
   qaz741wsd856/frp (TXT parsing, Apache-2.0).

4) frp -- https://github.com/fatedier/frp
   Copyright The frp Authors
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   This product implements the documented frp wire protocol and accepts the frp
   configuration file format for interoperability. No source code from that
   project is contained in this distribution.

