is in `Cargo.lock` (and the direct dependency declarations in `Cargo.toml` and
the Cargo.toml files of the `common`, `server` and `client` crates). Notable
direct dependencies include:

  - tokio, tokio-util, futures      (MIT)
  - quinn, quinn-proto              (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - rustls, tokio-rustls, rcgen     (Apache-2.0 OR MIT / MIT)
  - ring                            (ISC-style; see the crate's LICENSE)
  - clap                            (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - anyhow                          (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - tracing, tracing-subscriber     (MIT)
  - serde, toml, bytes, base64      (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  - rand, sha2, aes-gcm, hkdf, md-5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes in this distribution

  - `common/src/ip4p.rs` (new): IP4P client-side endpoint resolution + cache.
  - `common/src/dns.rs`: TXT / AAAA query support and OS DNS server discovery.
  - `client/src/main.rs`: IP4P applied to TCP/WS/WSS/KCP/QUIC dial paths;
    WSS now sends a standard TLS ClientHello (no frp custom first byte).
  - `server/src/serve.rs`: second-level WebSocket probe after TLS => native
    same-port WSS; peeked bytes are always replayed for non-WebSocket clients.
  - `server/build.rs`, `client/build.rs`, `scripts/gen_winres.py`,
    `assets/winres/*.res`: Windows VERSIONINFO + asInvoker manifest.
  - Docs, CI and release workflows.

